===persian===

باغبان، سبز شدن را،
به گیاه نمی‌آموزد...
باغبان،
نشانی بهار را به دانه...
و... نامهٔ باران را به سبزه می‌دهد...
نمی‌توان، به پرنده یاد داد، که...
در کویر... یا... برگ بید... لانه بسازد...
من باغبانم...
اگر دانهٔ شوقی در توست...
آن را خواهم رویاند...
در کارگاه حجم سبز ۱۳۷۲

===machine===

The gardener does not teach
the plant how to go green...
The gardener
gives the seed the address of spring...
and... gives the grass the letter of the rain...
You cannot teach a bird to...
build its nest... in the desert... or... on a willow leaf...
I am a gardener...
If there is a seed of longing in you...
I will bring it up...
At the Green Volume workshop, 1372

===lantern===

A gardener does not teach the plant
how to go green.
A gardener
hands the seed the address of spring
and hands the grass the letter of the rain.
You cannot teach a bird
to build its nest in the desert, or on a willow leaf.
I am a gardener.
If there is a seed of longing in you,
I will bring it up...

At the Green Volume workshop, 1372

===translation===

===footnotes===

*The Green Volume* — حجم سبز — is Sohrab Sepehri's 1967 collection, and the workshop in the
dateline is named after it. The poem is about teaching, written from a room named for another
poet's book, by a man who says a teacher can only give directions and wait.
